<.layout_page_centered>
  <!-- Project header -->
  <.container_page_heading
    title="NativeDSD"
    description="Getting you closer to the original performance"
  />
  <!-- Brand hero image -->
  <.container_hero_image image="/images/cases/nativedsd_home.png" />
  <!-- About company -->
  <.container_page_text title="The Company">
    <.container_page_paragraph>
      <.link_styled href="https://nativedsd.com">NativeDSD</.link_styled>
      is a music platform for ultra high-end audiophiles — customers who invest tens of thousands of dollars in specialised equipment to hear the difference. Content is sold via one-time purchases, subscriptions, and streaming.
    </.container_page_paragraph>
    <.container_page_paragraph>
      Every file is delivered in lossless, multi-channel studio quality — 10–20x larger than a standard Spotify track.
      The platform stores & delivers hundreds of TB of audio on a monthly basis.
    </.container_page_paragraph>
  </.container_page_text>
  
<!-- About project -->
  <.container_page_text title="The project">
    <.container_page_paragraph>
      NativeDSD 1.0 launched in the early 2010s and due to it's success it has outgrown their early
      tech stack & infrastructure. Our work consisted in building NativeDSD 2.0 on a new tech & infra stack.
    </.container_page_paragraph>
  </.container_page_text>

  <.container_box_large
    alignment="right"
    image="/images/cases/nativedsd_about.png"
    title="Infra & tech stack"
  >
    <div>
      <h3 class="font-semibold">Before</h3>
      <ul>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-minus">
          no CI/CD pipeline & no containers
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-minus">
          self hosted Wordpress shop (heavily customised with plugins)
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-minus">
          a custom <.link_styled href="https://www.php.net/">PHP</.link_styled> backoffice with legacy framework
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-minus">
          a desktop app written in JS / Atom Electron
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="font-semibold py-4">After</h3>
      <ul>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          <.link_styled href="https://www.docker.com/">Docker</.link_styled> containers & full automated CI/CD & test/prod envs
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          <.link_styled href="https://www.docker.com/">Docker</.link_styled> containers & full automated CI/CD & test/prod envs
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>

        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          Shopify based shop (customised with minimal plugins)
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>

        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          completely rewritten platform/backoffice in <.link_styled href="https://www.php.net/">PHP</.link_styled>/<.link_styled href="https://laravel.com/">Laravel</.link_styled> with async first architecture
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>

        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          completely rewritten desktop app with <.link_styled href="https://www.php.net/">PHP</.link_styled>/<.link_styled href="https://laravel.com/">Laravel</.link_styled>
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </.container_box_large>
  <.container_box_large
    alignment="left"
    image="/images/cases/nativedsd_albums_dashboard.png"
    title="5x cheaper data strage & delivery"
  >
    <p>
      The main operation cost for NativeDSD is data storage & traffic.
      We discovered that NativeDSD had very specific storage and delivery needs and AWS forced us to pay a lot for many features we didn't actually use. A hybrid approach (AWS, Hetzner, Bunny) was the right fit at much lower costs.
    </p>
    <div>
      <h3 class="font-semibold py-4">Before</h3>
      <ul>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-minus">
          <.link_styled href="https://aws.amazon.com/">AWS</.link_styled> compute & database
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-minus">
          <.link_styled href="https://aws.amazon.com/s3/">AWS S3</.link_styled> storage & <.link_styled href="https://aws.amazon.com/cloudfront/">Cloudfront</.link_styled> data delivery
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="font-semibold py-4">After</h3>
      <ul>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          <.link_styled href="https://aws.amazon.com/">AWS</.link_styled> database + <.link_styled href="https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/">AWS Outpost</.link_styled> (managed dockers for bare metal)
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          <.link_styled href="https://www.hetzner.com/">Hetzner</.link_styled> bare metal compute
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          <.link_styled href="https://www.hetzner.com/">Hetzner</.link_styled> bare bones data storage
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          <.link_styled href="https://aws.amazon.com/s3/storage-classes/glacier/">AWS Glacier</.link_styled> for long term backups
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          <.link_styled href="https://bunny.net/">Bunny CDN</.link_styled> data delivery
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </.container_box_large>
  
<!--Numbers achieved -->
  <div class="relative flex flex-col justify-between space-y-10 px-10
    md:px-6 md:space-y-0 md:space-x-7 md:flex-row my-10">
    <.container_box_small
      title="5x"
      subtitle="less cost"
    />
    <.container_box_small
      title="2x"
      subtitle="more albums"
    />
    <.container_box_small
      title="3x"
      subtitle="speed increase"
    />
  </div>
  <!--Quote -->
  <.container_page_card
    description="Remote Reason has improved the site's speed and backend functionality. The team has facilitated a structured and
    precise workflow, delivered weekly reports every Monday, and communicated via calls, chats, and meetings. They've also created steps to simplify the problem and
    craft a clear solution."
    image={LinkHelper.image_path("/cases/jonas.jpeg")}
    name="Jonas Sacks"
    position="CEO, NativeDSD Music"
    linkedin="https://nl.linkedin.com/in/jonas-sacks-7aa771271"
    clutch="https://clutch.co/go-to-review/21913110-da3a-48cc-9200-43ae5de59e57/380383"
  />
  <!--Showcase -->
  <.lets_talk_cta />

  <div class="mt-16 container px-6 lg:px-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-normal text-left md:text-4xl">
      NativeDSD 2.0
    </h1>
  </div>
  <!-- Boxes -->
  <.container_box_large
    alignment="right"
    image="/images/cases/nativedsd_details.png"
    title="Shop 2.0 - Shopify"
  >
    <ul>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        We migrated all the old shop data & integrations from <.link_styled href="https://wordpress.org/">Wordpress</.link_styled> (with <.link_styled href="https://woocommerce.com/">Woocommerce</.link_styled>) to <.link_styled href="https://www.shopify.com/">Shopify</.link_styled>. This included integrations like payment provider (<.link_styled href="https://stripe.com/">Stripe</.link_styled> & <.link_styled href="https://www.mollie.com/">Mollie</.link_styled>), <.link_styled href="https://www.intercom.com/">Intercom</.link_styled>, <.link_styled href="https://mailchimp.com/">Mailchimp</.link_styled> and others.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        The platform synchronises with Shopify (via webhooks and REST APIs).
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        Custom Shopify embedded apps (for customers & admins)
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        Search Engine Optimisations. Agentic Engine Optimisations.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
    </ul>
  </.container_box_large>
  <.container_box_large
    alignment="left"
    image="/images/cases/nativedsd_about.png"
    title="Platform 2.0 - Custom"
  >
    <ul>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        The newly built NativeDSD platform keeps all it's master data (users, customers, purchases, albums, subscriptions, etc) in it's core platform.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        The platform exposes audio data (with signed urls) and metadata via REST APIs. These API endpoints are used by external systems (Shopify, Desktop catalog app, Streaming brokers) to deliver services to the NativeDSD customers.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        Additionally the platform is responsible for audio data collection delivered via FTP by partner labels and also automated long term backups at scale.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
    </ul>
  </.container_box_large>
  <.container_box_large
    alignment="right"
    image="/images/cases/nativedsd_labels_dashboard.png"
    title="Backoffice 2.0"
  >
    <ul>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        The newly built backoffice is used by the NativeDSD team to automate the importing of data, manage products & publish to Shopify.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        Additionally the web portal has separate modules used by the partner labels (ie. organisations that record and publish albums) to validate, fix and deliver their audio files to resell them via the NativeDSD main shop.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
    </ul>
  </.container_box_large>
  <.container_box_large
    alignment="left"
    image="/images/cases/nativedsd_search.png"
    title="Desktop app 2.0"
  >
    <ul>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <b>Cross-Platform</b>
        Available on macOS, Windows, and Linux. Files are sorted into clean SKU → album → resolution folders, with full catalog search by album, artist, or track.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <b>
          Reliable Download Management
        </b>
        Downloads queue automatically with pause support. Network interruptions are detected and resumed, with bulk "Resume All" and "Retry All Failed" actions.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <b>
          Multi-Format Downloads
        </b>
        Download all your purchased DSD, FLAC, and WAV music. Choose quality per album, skip individual tracks, and optionally include artwork and booklets.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
    </ul>
  </.container_box_large>
  <!-- Project Highlights  -->
  <.container_page_text title="Highlights" />
  <.container_page_box>
    <.page_box_items title="Project">
      <p class="font-semibold">
        Sector: <span class="font-normal">Arts, entertainment &amp music </span>
      </p>
      <p class="font-semibold">
        Work: <span class="font-normal">Backend, Frontend, Devops </span>
      </p>
      <p class="font-semibold">
        Size: <span span class="font-normal"> > 2 000 h </span>
      </p>
    </.page_box_items>
    <.page_box_items title="Verticals">
      <p>- Streaming</p>
      <p>- Big data</p>
      <p>- E-commerce</p>
    </.page_box_items>
    <.page_box_items title="Technologies">
      <p>
        - <.tech_icon name="php" /> PHP / <.tech_icon name="laravel" /> Laravel /
        <.tech_icon name="js" /> JS
      </p>
      <p>
        - <.tech_icon name="aws" /> AWS / <.tech_icon name="hetzner" /> Hetzner /
        <.tech_icon name="docker" /> Docker
      </p>
      <p>- <.tech_icon name="shopify" /> Shopify / <.tech_icon name="wordpress" /> Wordpress</p>
    </.page_box_items>
  </.container_page_box>
</.layout_page_centered>
